<!--
  Two Franka Panda arms playing air hockey, for replaying the Isaac-Lab-trained hierarchical
  agents (Isaac-Franka-Soccer-Hierarchical). GENERATED by assets/make_franka_hockey_xml.py --
  edit that script (and shared/franka_transfer_cfg.py for the physics knobs), not this file.

  Kinematics / inertias / meshes: MuJoCo Menagerie franka_emika_panda (the franka_description
  URDF Isaac's panda_instanceable.usd comes from). Bodies and joints carry the Isaac names with
  a me_/foe_ prefix; the policy<->sim mapping is by name.

  Control: Isaac's implicit PD (FRANKA_PANDA_HIGH_PD_CFG: kp 400 / kd 80, effort 87 for joints
  1-4 and 12 for 5-7; fingers kp 2000 / kd 100 held at 0) as <position> actuators, integrated
  with implicitfast so the kv damping is implicit like PhysX's. Arm links are gravity
  compensated (Isaac spawns them with disable_gravity=True). No self-collision (Isaac
  enabled_self_collisions=False): contype/conaffinity bits
    me robot   contype=1 conaffinity=14    foe robot  contype=2 conaffinity=13
    table/rails contype=4 conaffinity=11   puck contype=8 conaffinity=7
  The puck's per-DoF damping (PhysX linear 0.25 / angular 2.0) is written by the env at load, and
  the env applies PhysX-style restitution to the puck explicitly (rails 0.9, table 0.225, arms
  0.35, bounce threshold 0.2 m/s): the MuJoCo contacts here are stiff and critically damped.

  Colors are the Isaac play clip's: white shell, dark trim repainted per side (me blue, foe
  red), dark green table, light grey rails, green/red goal zones, yellow puck.
-->
